{"user": "what does legal mean in regards to the game", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T13:08:20.072750+00:00", "assistant": "A **legal move** in Othello means:\n\n- You place a disc on an **empty square**\n- That move must **trap at least one White disc** in a straight line \u2014 horizontal, vertical, or diagonal\n- There must be one of your **Black discs at the far end**\n- The trapped White discs then flip to Black\n\nIf you have **no legal moves**, you must **pass**.  \nIn this board, there are **0 empty squares**, so the game is over.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T13:08:25.779960+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T13:08:27.157838+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
