{"user": "is the concept the same each game", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T13:10:25.648706+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 the **basic concept is the same every game**:\n\n- Place Black discs to **trap and flip** White discs.\n- If you have **no legal move**, you **pass**.\n- When the board is full or neither player can move, the game ends.\n- Winner = **most discs at the end**.\n\nBut the **best strategy changes each position**: corners, mobility, and avoiding giving White good moves matter more than just flipping many discs.\n\nHere the board is full, so the game is over: **White 42, Black 22**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T13:10:30.167027+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T13:10:32.038109+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
